From 40e91500bfed8c2a9f7c48092ef8d8e7b4be095f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:04:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): flush the worker's text answer before the
 stop-loop nudge's next request [daveey]

The kanban stop guard appended a worker's text-only final answer as ephemeral
scaffolding (_kanban_stop_synthetic) and continued straight into the next model
request without flushing it. An observed managed worker (Ask Eve's private
observer binds every SDK response to exactly one durable assistant row before
the next SDK request) therefore faulted closed with "previous response never
durably bound", and every retry hit "SDK request after observer close/fault".

Match verify-on-stop and pre_verify: the answer goes through
_append_interim_answer (emit + append + session-DB flush, finish_reason
kanban_terminal_required kept); only the nudge row carries
_kanban_stop_synthetic. The finalizer now drops that nudge with the other
verification-continuation nudges, and compaction anchoring treats it as
synthetic user scaffolding, so budget exhaustion keeps exactly one answer row.

Tests: tests/agent/test_kanban_stop_interim_flush.py (RED on main, GREEN here):
the answer row is in state.db when the second request is made, the nudge is
never persisted, and budget exhaustion leaves one durable answer.

Ask Eve's pinned core (1f926111b0fa) is not touched; it picks this up with its
next core pin.
